; Evaluation is f64 and the ONE narrowing to f32 happens at write-buffer
; encode — so a value that does not fit f32 would land as ±inf. The
; `(repr-shape :type f32)` on the kinds that narrow refuses it at
; compile: `:value` is typed by the `key-value` UNION, so its record is
; union_no_branch_matched (a union forwards no branch's private cause);
; `:t` is typed by the bare `stage-weight`, so its record is
; repr_out_of_range. Both carry a span on the offending literal.
(transport :bpm 120)

(track :target radius
  (key :at 0b :value 1e39)
  (key :at 1b :value 1 :ease (seq (stage :ease linear :t 1e39 :v 1))))
